## 8. Known Limitations & Design Decisions

### 8.1 Default Procedure Selection

**Decision:** When an Ultrasound category is selected, the system returns the **first procedure** in the array (typically the most comprehensive option).

**Example:**
- Pregnancy Ultrasound → Returns CPT 76801 (First Trimester)
- User may actually need CPT 76805 (Second/Third Trimester) or CPT 76815 (Limited)

**Rationale:** 
- Ultrasound has no contrast options to differentiate procedures
- Returning the most comprehensive scan is safer (covers more anatomy)
- Alternative would require an additional selection step (similar to X-Ray views)

### 8.2 Regional Subcategories Not Implemented

**Current:** Each category has 3 procedures, but user cannot choose between them

**Future Enhancement:** Add secondary selection UI:
```
Pregnancy Ultrasound (OB) →
  ├── First Trimester (6-13 weeks)
  ├── Second/Third Trimester (14-40 weeks)
  └── Limited/Follow-up
```

### 8.3 Cross-Server Communication

**Architecture:** Astro (localhost:3000) submits to Remix (localhost:5173)

**Production Consideration:** Ensure `remixUrl` environment variable is configured correctly in production deployment

